+//! Where a question about the store is answered.
+//!
+//! `lakelet/4.10-downsampling` opens this module, and what it answers is the first question
+//! anybody asks of a telemetry store: not "give me every sample" but *"how did this move"*. A
+//! dashboard wants a point a minute, an alert wants a point an hour, and a year of one-second
+//! samples is thirty million records nobody wants to read — so a query is almost never about
+//! records. It is about **windows** of time, and every window is a bucket of the absolute time
+//! axis rather than of the data (`[`downsample::Window`]`).
+//!
+//! Three things are deliberately absent from everything below:
+//!
+//! * **a file and a store.** Which segments an answer may read, and what a query may ask for, is
+//!   `lakelet/4.11-query-engine`'s; this module is handed records and answers about them.
+//! * **a clock.** A window is a width and a range is two numbers, both passed in — so the same
+//!   question answers the same way on every machine and in every process.
+//! * **a side effect.** Everything here is a value in and a value out, which is what lets a spec
+//!   name a bucket boundary instead of hoping for one.
+
+// The steps that come after this one add their own files here — the grammar, the parser, the plan
+// and the executor of `lakelet/4.11-query-engine` are the next four — and a scaffold may only
+// write inside a `kiln:scaffold:begin`/`kiln:scaffold:end` region (docs/authoring.md §5).
+// kiln:scaffold:begin
+// `lakelet/4.10-downsampling`: the window arithmetic and the five aggregates, as a pure function
+// over records.
+pub mod downsample;
+// kiln:scaffold:end
